  "principles": [
    "Default to plain language and spell out uncommon terms on first use: Full Term (ACRONYM).",
    "Acronyms (and initialisms/brevity codes) and abbreviations (truncations/contractions) are distinct: never define standard abbreviations in parentheses.",
    "Do not capitalize expanded words merely because the acronym is all caps (e.g., on-the-job training [OJT], operations security [OPSEC]).",
    "When an acronym has multiple meanings across commands or AFSCs, spell out on first use or pin the intended meaning in unit_style.json."
